---
description: Keep app/ limited to routes and route-specific UI
globs: app/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# app/ — routes only

Allowed files: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `global-error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `route.ts`, and UI used on that route only.

- Group routes: `app/(auth)/`, `app/(dashboard)/`, `app/(marketing)/`
- If a component is used on more than one route, move it to `components/`
- Pages fetch via `data/` in Server Components — never call Supabase here
- Mutations go through `actions/`, not inline in pages
- Every data-fetching route gets a colocated `loading.tsx` with `RouteSkeleton` (boneyard-js) and a shadcn fallback layout. Next shows it automatically while the Server Component loads. Do not fake this with `useState` + Skeleton on first paint.
- Errors use the shared `ErrorScreen` / `RouteError` UI. Do not leave Next’s default error page.
  - `error.tsx` in each route group so the parent layout (navbar / sidebar) stays
  - `app/error.tsx` as a fallback
  - `app/global-error.tsx` for root-layout failures — must include `<html>` + `<body>`, fonts, and `globals.css`
  - `app/not-found.tsx` for unknown URLs and `notFound()`

```
app/
├── error.tsx
├── global-error.tsx
├── not-found.tsx
├── (auth)/login/page.tsx
├── (dashboard)/projects/
│   ├── page.tsx
│   └── loading.tsx   ← RouteSkeleton + shadcn fallback for this route
└── api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts
```

Top-of-screen progress on route changes is `NextTopLoader` in `app/layout.tsx`, not a per-route component. Keep `TooltipProvider` wrapped around `{children}` there as well (shadcn tooltip).
